{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>תֻּמַּת</b> — on the pattern of טֻמְאַת; the proper form is תֻּמַּת." "<b>תְנַחֵם</b> — that they not stumble." "<b>וְסָלֶף</b> — distortion, that is, that others will distort." "<b>יְשֻׁדֵּם</b> — the slief, it will destroy those traitors. And this is the interpretation according to the qere with yod. And according to the qere with vav: 'and slief comes to traitors,' and [it is read] וְשָׁדַד אוֹתָם הַסָּלֶף."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {3 "The text reads 'הסלף' (the slief) as subject of 'ישודו'; translated hyper-literally as printed. 'סלף' (slief) left untranslated as Ibn Ezra's term for distortion/crookedness. The second qere reading appears garbled in the witnesses; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:07.736731646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}